  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses solely on the probability of loss, and in this case, the individual does consider the fact that Lottery B has a significant chance of loss (‘ein Verlust von 3000€ ebenso wahrscheinlich’), which contributes to their decision. However, the verbal report also includes considerations beyond loss probability—specifically expected value and outcome magnitude—which are not part of the given decision reason. While the lower probability of loss in A aligns with the reason, the individual’s justification is broader and includes additional criteria. Therefore, although the probability of loss is mentioned and plays a role, it is not clear that it was the decisive factor in the way the decision reason prescribes. The match between the reason’s rule and the individual’s justification is partial.",
